WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.420
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:31.650
Kaiba!

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.370
I know you just lost, but duel me!

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.950
Let's see who finishes third!

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.990
A single defeat won't stop my road to becoming a true duelist!

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.890
What?  A virus combo already?

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:51.560
My deck now only has monsters with low attack points.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.090
But the duel is only getting started!

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Blue-Eyes White Dragon vs Blue-Eyes White Dragon

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.260
How's that, Kaiba?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.710
I didn't win in Battle City for nothing!

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.940
Nice, Jonouchi!

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.450
He's keeping up with Kaiba!

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.320
Jonouchi has grown as a duelist.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.330
Yeah!  Jonouchi is stronger now!

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:32.770
If Marik didn't start a Shadow Game, Jonouchi would've won the semifinals.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.150
Return, Phoenix!

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.000
What?

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.110
W-Why?

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:58.130
Is Jonouchi's emotional strength stronger than God's attack?

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.560
My... turn...

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.960
I draw...

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.970
Yugi.  I...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.020
Gearfried...

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:16.950
I win.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.880
Attac-

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:34.750
Jonouchi would've defeated Marik if he was able to attack.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.260
Yeah.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:42.220
When Battle City is over, I will duel Jonouchi, as promised.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.140
I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.890
Yeah!  It will be a great duel!

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.510
That means we must defeat Marik.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.090
Yeah.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.110
I will win!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.380
My brother's virus combo didn't work?

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.320
Jonouchi is playing well.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.680
Seems you learned how to use your brain.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.850
But not very well.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.770
Say what!

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.170
Even if you survive this turn...

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:17.080
...due to Crush Card Virus, you have no monsters with at least 1500 attack points in your deck.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.920
You can't rely on luck forever.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:23.820
It's true that I can't use my strongest monsters...

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.080
...like Panther Warrior and Rocket Warrior.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:32.230
But I can't give up and run away!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:36.320
I will defeat you and fulfill my promise with Yugi!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.120
Hang in there, Jonouchi!

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.130
Once a fool, always a fool.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:48.130
Fine!  I'll show that your strength is nowhere near mine!

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.270
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:53.100
I summon Blade Knight in attack position!

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.560
Attack Swordsman of Landstar!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.110
Destroy that weakling!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.810
He destroyed it and turned the tables!

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.440
Was Jonouchi just lucky before?

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.360
No.  Jonouchi won't lose like this.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.500
I set one card.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.670
I end my turn.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.020
The duel is only getting started!

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.310
Here I go!

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:39.080
What did they see back then?

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.000
What's this?

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.480
The Millennium Rod is glowing again.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.400
What?  What's going on?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.940
Why did it only react to them?

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.200
I'm the owner of the Millennium Rod!

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.200
Rod!  Show me what you showed them!

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.220
You're...

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.570
My turn!

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:36.700
I draw!

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.050
Here I go!

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.500
I summon Little-Winguard in attack position!

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.070
What's he doing?

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:52.360
1400 attack points are less than Kaiba's Blade Knight!

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:56.600
He's supposed to protect his life points by using defense position!

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.000
What are you thinking?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.400
Is a scrub using scrub-like strategies?

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.440
Maybe.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.320
I'll also play this!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.200
The Equip Spell, Legendary Sword!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:14.110
The equipped monster gains 300 attack and defense points.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:17.510
Nice!  It now has 1700 attack points!

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:19.450
More than Blade Knight!

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.660
I equip Legendary Sword on Little-Winguard!

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.530
I flip over my set card!

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.780
Absorb Spell.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.900
What?

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.800
When a spell raises your monster's attack points...

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.620
...Absorb Spell transfers those points to my monster instead.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.360
My Legendary Sword...

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.710
None of your tricks will work on me.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.500
You're just a weak scrub of a duelist.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.400
Stop calling me a scrub!

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.420
I set one card!

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.590
I end my turn!

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:02.590
It's frustrating, but Kaiba is really tough.

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:05.590
Yeah.  But look.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:08.300
Jonouchi hasn't given up.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.230
Because he doesn't know how to give up.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.260
What are you thinking, girl?

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:19.560
That doesn't belong to you.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.830
Hand it over!

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.400
Why did the Millennium Rod...

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.350
You're...!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:36.460
What?

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:38.260
My other self!

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:42.570
The Millennium Puzzle is reacting to something.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.660
Does it have to do with Marik?

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:48.470
Anzu!

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.970
No way!  Is Anzu in trouble?

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:54.680
Come to think of it, she's still gone.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.410
Do your best, Jonouchi.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:06.020
I thought I could win with the Equip Spell.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:09.050
But I powered up Kaiba's monster instead.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.030
If he attacks me...

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.970
My turn!

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.220
I draw!

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:22.280
I'll crush you so completely that you'll never think of challenging me to a duel again!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.810
I activate the spell card, Enemy Controller!

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.250
By paying 1000 life points...

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:39.990
...I can input a code to take control of your monster.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.900
Kaiba is willing to risk paying 1000 life points?

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.930
He wants to end this right now.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.940
Left!  Right!  A!  B!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.050
My controller activates!

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.870
I've captured Little-Winguard!

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.740
I activate a spell from my hand.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.200
Cost Down!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.680
Its effect lowers the Level of a monster in my hand by 2.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.770
It can't be!

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.690
A Level 8 monster usually requires two tributes...

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:15.310
...but I can summon it with only one tribute!

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:21.400
I'll show you the overwhelming difference in our power!

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.020
I tribute Little-Winguard!

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.570
Come out, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:58.200
It's a waste to play this against a scrub.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:02.340
But you should feel honored to lose against Blue-Eyes!

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.270
This is bad!  Jonouchi has no monsters on his field!

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.220
Go, Blue-Eyes!

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.710
Attack Jonouchi directly!

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:12.880
Jonouchi!

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.190
Jonouchi!

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.050
I won't let you!

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:18.910
I flip over my set card!

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.360
Scapegoat!

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.190
What?

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.630
I won't lose that easily!

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:33.440
Jonouchi!  Stop scaring us!

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:36.140
That was close, but he survived!

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:40.680
You can't deal me damage unless you destroy my Scapegoats!

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.840
Then I'll mow you down with strength!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.280
Go, Blade Knight!

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:53.940
What?  Blade Knight gained attack points!

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.040
It's one of Blade Knight's effects.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.600
When I have one or fewer cards in my hand, it gains 400 attack points.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.340
Blue-Eyes has 3000 attack points.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:08.460
Blade Knight has 2300 attack points.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:13.220
My virus combo only lets you summon monsters with 1500 or lower attack points.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.280
There's no hope for you.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:21.050
If nothing changes, Kaiba will destroy my Scapegoats on his next turn.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.350
I end my turn.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.160
Isn't there anything I can do?

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.460
I'm counting on you!

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.060
No good.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.000
All I can do for now is survive.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.470
I set a card!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.580
I summon Battle Warrior in defense position.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:43.900
I end my turn!

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.890
You fight in vain.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.200
You don't know that!

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:52.550
I see.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:57.220
A fragment of your memories is inside her.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.460
I won't let you do whatever you like!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.310
Sure about this?

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:08.480
I know you didn't forget that this is also your body.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.600
I know.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:14.030
But this is the only way to stop you!

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.820
So you're that desperate.

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:20.860
But this will make your sister sad.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.820
Rishido too.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:29.350
What will he do when he learns that he couldn't protect you?

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:30.950
Rishido...

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:36.080
This is why I say you have a weak endgame!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.260
I've turned the tables.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:50.670
You shouldn't have showed up.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.030
Oh my.  You're so nimble.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.350
However!

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:24.070
A memory fragment can never oppose me!

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.510
You're the one who should vanish!

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:33.780
Vanish!

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:36.340
Stop!

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.320
If it isn't my sister.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:48.760
Sis!

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.280
Marik, pull yourself together!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.270
Sorry.  I can't...

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:54.600
Marik!

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:57.080
Forget about me.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.710
Defeat him...

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.590
Marik!

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:04.490
What's with that, Sister?

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:07.350
I'm the one who was almost erased.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:09.960
You're no fun.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.290
Should I get rid of you too?

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.860
There's no way you can protect yourself.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:19.660
Stop it!

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:25.460
Oh my.  A lot of interruptions today.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.770
Marik, I won't let you meddle any further!

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.000
Really?  How?

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.260
Want to battle right now?

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:49.600
Forget it.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.020
Fighting now will be boring.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:56.220
I have a better stage in mind.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.980
I'll save my fun for later.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.110
Just you wait!

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.220
My other self, Anzu is...

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:14.250
Anzu!

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:15.570
Anzu!

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.250
She's fine.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.250
She only passed out.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.450
Why is Anzu here?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.860
Yugi, I have a favor to ask you.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:28.310
Me?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.960
Please save my brother Marik!

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:39.140
My turn.  I draw.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.480
The spell card, Card of Demise!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.650
I  draw until I have five cards in my hand.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.680
A card that replenishes his hand!

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:55.690
In exchange for getting cards now, I must discard my entire hand five turns later.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:59.600
But I don't have to worry about that happening in this duel.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:01.730
What do you mean by that!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.560
It means I'll end this quickly.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:08.170
I summon Kaiser Sea Horse in attack position!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.300
I'll eradicate your weaklings!

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.020
Then Blade Knight!

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:27.420
Destroy the last one, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:29.960
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:36.140
Jonouchi's monsters are gone in an instant!

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:39.870
He can't stop Kaiba's attack next turn!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.700
I end my turn.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.120
But there's nothing left to protect you.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.520
Continuing will be a waste of time.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:50.070
Hurry up and surrender.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.420
I'll never surrender!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:58.660
I'll never give up in a duel as long as I have cards in my deck!

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:01.290
You're just being stubborn, scrub.

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:02.740
Be quiet!

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.720
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:07.660
I still have a chance!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.460
Pot of Greed let me draw two cards.

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:14.560
C'mon!  This time!

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:17.900
Yeah!  This works!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.840
I activate my set card!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.700
Graverobber!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.200
Kaiba!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.160
I took a card from your graveyard!

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:27.950
What?

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:31.620
The card is... Enemy Controller.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:39.770
By paying 1000 life points, I can input a code to take control of your monster.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:45.560
But there's another code I can input.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:51.840
Up!   Left!  Down!  Right!

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.770
A!

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:56.460
This code destroys your monster!

00:18:58.530 --> 00:18:59.310
Can't be!

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:01.410
Blue-Eyes explodes!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.910
I'm not done.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.100
I activate Monster Reborn!

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:09.850
What?

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.570
And of course, I resurrect...

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:15.480
Come out, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:22.470
This is Graverobber and Monster Reborn's ultimate combo!

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.650
Well done, Jonouchi!

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:26.180
That strategy is great!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.000
He might win!

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:29.410
Brother...

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:35.120
Blue-Eyes attacks Blade Knight!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:37.380
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:42.350
How dare you!

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:46.310
I summon Hayabusa Knight in defense position!

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:50.860
This is my last move!  I set a card!

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:53.000
I end my turn!

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.370
How's that?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.970
You never know what happens in a duel.

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:59.660
That's why I never give up and keep fighting!

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:04.380
How dare you make my Blue-Eyes obey you!

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:06.870
I won't forgive you for humiliating me!.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:14.920
Blue-Eyes, I'd rather destroy you than let Jonouchi control you.

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:21.310
If I tribute Kaiser Sea Horse to summon a Light Attribute monster...

00:20:21.310 --> 00:20:25.200
...I need one less monster to tribute.

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:29.970
Since Blue-Eyes is Light Attribute,  I can summon it with only one tribute.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:31.900
No way!  Another one?

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:34.910
I tribute Kaiser Sea Horse.

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:38.780
Come out, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:48.850
How's that, scrub?

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.290
Another Blue-Eyes!

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:56.350
Die together!

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:59.400
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:11.040
Damn!  He's unbelievable!

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:16.200
Has he gone mad because he's upset that I took his Blue-Eyes?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.120
My turn isn't over yet.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:23.150
You're not the only one who can revive the dead.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:24.120
What?

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:25.860
Monster Reborn.

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.390
Resurrect, Blue-Eyes!

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:30.390
Return to your true owner!

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:37.370
Kaiba also had Monster Reborn in his hand?

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:41.040
You'll never use Blue-Eyes to its full potential!

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:47.070
Now that Blue-Eyes has returned to its rightful owner, feel its terror!

00:21:54.720 --> 00:22:00.350
Jonouchi used Monster Reborn to take Kaiba's Blue-Eyes and counterattack.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:04.170
But it was taken right back, so he's in a pinch again!

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:07.970
But the good thing about Jonouchi is that he never gives up.

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:12.300
Surviving Kaiba's overwhelming attack, he draws...

00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:16.420
...Time Wizard, the card that got him out of trouble many times!

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:18.550
Now can he beat Kaiba?

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:21.250
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Road to Becoming a True Duelist

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:23.250
Duel, standby!

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:38.950
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:39.450 --> 00:22:47.290
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:49.020 --> 00:22:58.450
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:59.070 --> 00:23:07.970
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:17.000
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:22.510
I'll live feeling them

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:27.690
For me to be me

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:36.150
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:41.790
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:51.450
We'll both understand that someday
